title: "Parker's 5-minute peaks turn up just as often at other frequencies"
abstract: "Three pre-registered tests of the reported \"~6 sigma\" in situ sighting of the Sun's 5-minute oscillations all come out at the chance level. Peaks that large appear as often at control frequencies, the 3 mHz band is not special across 3,931 windows, and the two published peaks have false-alarm probabilities of 1.5 % and 0.29 % in their own windows. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
